<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phuntsog Namgyal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1604">1604</a>–<a href="/years/1670">1670</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phuntsog Namgyal was the first Chogyal, or king, of Sikkim, consecrated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuksom">Yuksom</a> in 1642 by three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhist</a> lamas. Founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namgyal-dynasty">Namgyal dynasty</a>, he organised a Buddhist monarchy over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhutia">Bhutia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lepcha">Lepcha</a> peoples and set up the administration of the kingdom. His dynasty ruled Sikkim until the monarchy was abolished in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phuntsog-namgyal.jpg" alt="Phuntsog Namgyal" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rangan Datta Wiki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Norbugang_8a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
